# GitHub synchronization

- After each completed change, run the relevant checks, commit the scoped project changes, and push the current branch to `origin` before ending the task.
- This is the user's standing authorization; do not ask again for routine commits and pushes.
- Keep secrets, local environments, build outputs, and generated reports out of commits. Respect `.gitignore`.
- Preserve unrelated work. Never force-push or discard changes to make a push succeed.
- Verify that the remote branch contains the local commit. Report any failed check or blocked push accurately; never claim synchronization without verification.
